{"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article","title":"Architecture & Performance","roleHeading":"Article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux relies on specific patterns to ensure correct ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" behavior, efficient rendering, and safe concurrency. This article explains the reasoning behind these patterns.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"The-Snapshot-Pattern","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The Snapshot Pattern"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" copies the observer tree into a local struct, mutates the copy via the reducer, then assigns changed properties back. This happens internally via ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"State(observer:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" packs, ","type":"text"},{"code":"State.apply(_:to:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" unpacks.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The pattern exists for two reasons:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" equality checking.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"type":"text","text":" accessor checks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" and suppresses no-op notifications. Swift’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_modify"},{"type":"text","text":" accessor (used by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout"},{"type":"text","text":") fires notifications unconditionally. The snapshot pattern routes through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Cross-slice observation isolation.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" macro generates a separate "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" class for each "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"type":"text","text":" property. A view reading "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.items"},{"type":"text","text":" won’t re-render when only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.ui"},{"type":"text","text":" changes, because they live on different observer objects."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" macro generates the observer class tree and ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance automatically. Hand-written conformance is still possible for advanced cases — see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxObservable","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"style":"note","name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Explicit equality guards ("},{"code":"if x != state.x { x = state.x }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") are unnecessary. "},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" already checks equality on "},{"code":"set","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Unconditional assignment is safe."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"},{"anchor":"Dispatch-Loop-Detection","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Dispatch Loop Detection"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"text":" warns if ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is called more than 100 times per debounce interval. This usually means ","type":"text"},{"code":"send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" isn’t using the snapshot pattern, causing cascading re-renders that trigger re-dispatches.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Reducer-Weight","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Reducer Weight"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers run synchronously on the MainActor. Move O(n²) work into an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and dispatch the result back as an action."}]},{"anchor":"Effect-Threading","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Effect Threading"},{"style":"important","name":"Important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Effects run on Swift concurrency’s cooperative thread pool via ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task { @concurrent in }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Blocking calls (","type":"text"},{"code":"Process.waitUntilExit()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"DispatchSemaphore.wait()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Thread.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") hold threads hostage. If enough block, the pool starves and the MainActor freezes.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use async alternatives: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"terminationHandler"},{"type":"text","text":" + continuation instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"waitUntilExit()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task.sleep()"},{"type":"text","text":" instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Thread.sleep()"},{"type":"text","text":", async file I\/O instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data(contentsOf:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}],"hierarc